\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Fifty source rotations, same partitions for all methods, TS on each rotation's Cal-A, one training seed per rotation. Risk: at the threshold for 80\% coverage fitted on Cal-B. LAC: coverage at nominal 0.90. LP: linear probe with class-weighted cross-entropy. Last four columns: LOTUS minus the row, and rotations where LOTUS is better. With three seeds, LOTUS against the MedSigLIP LP gives $+0.043$ bAcc (higher on 43/50) and lower ECE on 47/50 (Suppl.\nobreakspace  {}S6).}}{8}{table.1.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rot}{{5}{8}{Fifty source rotations, same partitions for all methods, TS on each rotation's Cal-A, one training seed per rotation. Risk: at the threshold for 80\% coverage fitted on Cal-B. LAC: coverage at nominal 0.90. LP: linear probe with class-weighted cross-entropy. Last four columns: LOTUS minus the row, and rotations where LOTUS is better. With three seeds, LOTUS against the MedSigLIP LP gives $+0.043$ bAcc (higher on 43/50) and lower ECE on 47/50 (\sups {6})}{table.1.5}{}}
